## Part L: fed-back accumulators

`for t in range(T): [acc = acc * alpha_t]; acc = tl.dot(p_t, v_t, acc)`, K = 64 per dot, every acc_t stored. `K loop`: tutorial 03 (p_t loaded in the format); `p.to`: tutorial 06 (p_t converted in registers from a softmax). Per dot, from the stored accumulator before it: the model against the device, each step against the step bound, the dot against errM. Whole chain (no rescale): the final result against errM over 4T chunks from the exact inputs (`whole errM ratio`); `bound / DotF16 composed`: errM over the whole chain divided by the bound a kernel gets by composing DotF16 step by step (e_{t+1} = e_t + relDot16(64) (|S_t| + e_t + L_t) + absDot16(64)), the largest over the elements.

